# Response headers for the static assets. Workers applies these to asset
# responses; the Worker's own routes (/upload, /i/*, /health) set their own,
# which is why stored images are not listed here — Cloudflare notes that
# `_headers` does not apply to Worker-generated responses.
#
# Without this file every asset is served with the default
# `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, so a returning visitor
# revalidates the shell and all ~38 files on every load. Vite gives hashed
# bundles under /assets/ names that change with their contents, so those can be
# cached indefinitely.

# The app shell, and every client-side route that serves it. Not cached: the
# shell references the hashed bundles, so a stale copy would pin a browser to a
# previous deploy.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Fingerprinted build output: the name changes when the content does.
#
# The detach line matters. Rules that both set a header are joined rather than
# overridden, so without it a bundle would be served
# `no-cache, public, max-age=31536000, immutable` — and no-cache would win,
# defeating the point. Detaching first makes this rule's value the only one.
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
